    "abstract": "Illustrated parts breakdown of one inner tank boost pump position, showing the inlet interface hardware keyed to the housing standard of the aircraft, the restrictor, the level sensing item and the local distribution parts.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of one inner tank boost pump position, including the inlet flange interface and the local distribution items. Use it to order pump interface hardware.",
      "figure_note": "The figure shows the left inner tank position looking outboard; the right hand side is a mirror image and the aircraft carries four positions in total. Items 10 and 10A are not alternates and must not be ordered against each other: the choice is fixed by the inlet housing standard of the aircraft and not by what is available. Item 10 is the restrictor at the outboard position introduced with the replacement inlet housing and is called up post MOD-145620; item 10A is the valve kit it replaced and is called up pre MOD-145620. Establish the embodiment status of the position before the order is raised. The flange seal is a single use item supplied with the pump and is not a separate catalogue item."
    },
